Beacon is not code-signed or notarized by Apple. Installing via Homebrew or the
install script clears the macOS quarantine flag for you; a manual DMG install
needs `xattr -cr /Applications/Beacon.app` once. That clears the extended
attributes on the app bundle and disables no other protection.

YOUR DATA

Beacon stores your work locally. No backups are kept for you, a forgotten Cloud
Sync passphrase cannot be recovered, and a collection you publish as a share is
public to anyone holding its link.

